    "notes": [
      "40 MHz operation is modeled as external synchronization of the BDS-MM, which supports sync-input frequencies from 20 to 50 MHz.",
      "Laser IRF width is set to 120 ps as a conservative 450 nm / 10 mW operating approximation from the BDS-MM family pulse-width table.",
      "Timing jitter field is set from the HPM-100-40 detector transit-time-spread specification (120 to 140 ps FWHM) as the practical system timing term.",
      "Dead time is set from the SPC-180NXX TCSPC module (80 ns). At 40 MHz this effectively prevents multihit operation, so event_multihit_capacity is set to 1.",
      "IRF position set to 0 ns because the requested profile defines 256 equal bins over the full 25 ns period."
    ]
  },
